<!-- Quick View Form on rev_applicant, showing Location Area (rev_locationarea) only. Built to
     close A-LOC-1 (EF-01, wbs:4.5), from ground truth read live 2026-09-23 by identity-agent
     against REV-GrantApplications-DEV (docs/development/quick-view-form-formxml-reference.md,
     "Shape 1"): <form hasmargin="false" shownavigationbar="false"> and a self-referencing
     <ancestor id> are the two attributes/elements that differ from a Main form; everything else
     is an ordinary form/tabs/columns/sections/rows/cell/control tree. classid on the field control
     is the same picklist classid rev_applicant's own main form already uses for rev_title/
     rev_gender ({3EF39988-22BB-4f0b-BBBE-64B5A3748AEE}) — rev_locationarea is a picklist
     (Entity.xml). Read-only rendering when embedded is a fixed platform property of the quick
     view control itself (Microsoft Learn, "Model-driven app quick view control properties":
     "The data displayed is not editable") — not something this form's own XML controls, and not
     dependent on the embedding control's ControlMode parameter. This form is deliberately
     single-field: EF-01/EF-38/EF-36 surface Location Area, Applicant Type and Age Range in three
     different, already-established form sections for three different reasons, so one shared
     multi-field Quick View Form would show two irrelevant fields in every section it appears in.
     A-QVF-1 (Dev Summary §10, CLOSED — WRONG): this file's root `<forms type>` attribute was
     hand-authored as "quickview" — an invented value, never ground-truthed, and it failed a live
     DEV import: "Forms being imported are of an unsupported type 'quickview' —
     Microsoft.Crm.Tools.ImportExportPublish.ImportFormXmlHandler.ImportItem" (IMP-0866). Per
     Microsoft Learn, "Customize entity forms" (developer/customize-dev/customize-entity-forms,
     form properties table), the FormXml `forms` element's `type` attribute takes the string
     values main, mobile, quickCreate and quick — NOT the numeric systemform.type enum (a
     different, unrelated vocabulary) and not "quickview". The sibling Main form on
     rev_application already establishes the string convention (`<forms type="main">`); the
     correct value for a Quick View Form is the string "quick". Corrected here.

     AND THE FOLDER NAME IS NOT A REPOSITORY PATH. This comment previously said the containing
     FormXml/quickview/ folder was "unaffected (it is a repository path, not a platform
     attribute)". That was never ground-truthed and is false: `pac solution pack` writes the
     packed customizations.xml <forms type> WRAPPER from the FormXml/<foldername>/ segment and
     never reads the attribute below, so this file stayed correct while every artifact built from
     it went on shipping type="quickview" to an import that had already rejected it (IMP-0874,
     reproduced with a real pack run). The folder was renamed to FormXml/quick/ to match. The
     two must agree; `verify-component-shape.py` now enforces that here, at source, and
     `verify-packed-form-types.py` re-checks it against the packed artifact. -->
